      "message": "The libx11-dev itself contains the headers and such (see https://packages.debian.org/sid/amd64/libx11-dev/filelist ), but does not provide any .so files (as you point out the one .so is actually a symlink). It does provide a .a file which appears to be a real file. This package then depends on other packages for which it provides those headers. (See https://packages.debian.org/sid/libx11-dev .) Is it possible the linker was finding the .a file to find the data to make the link work? It looks like linkers with -lfoo will look for libfoo.so preferentially (unless -static is specified) but failing that they will look for a libfoo.a.",
